Root cause
- powsimp.py had a code path that combined commutative power terms with base b and -b into (-1)**e plus base ** e when it thought sign extraction was safe. That code was permissive enough to apply to concrete numeric bases (like a = S(2)), which, combined with the subtle differences in numeric evaluation of negative base powers (branch cuts, internal normalization), caused simplify() to return an expression that evaluated numerically to a different complex value than the original product.

